(git tag v1.2.1, commit 6e8045d23ebaaba64136fe1fa211985bc0f85ec0; Go module
zip h1:+s9ZjMEjOB8NzZMVTM3cCenz2JrQIGGo5j1df19WjTA=), distributed under the
upstream MIT License in LICENSE, whose copyright notices are unchanged.

The fork's first commit is byte-identical to that release. The second changes
only the module path. The third carries two patches to the client package:

  1. client.NewWithOptions, which applies imap.Reader.MaxLiteralSize, Updates
     and ErrorLog before the greeting is read and before the reader goroutine
     starts. client.New is unchanged in behaviour and now calls it with no
     options.
  2. A recover in the client's reader loop, so a panic while handling a
     malformed server response closes the connection with an error instead of
     ending the process.
